---
description: Each test covers one edge case. Several assertions in that case are fine.
alwaysApply: true
---

# One edge case per test

A test is one edge case. Actor, starting point, action, every observable that belongs to that case. Split only when the edge case changes. Do not split one case into several tests that only differ by description.

Name, email, and company are three validations. Those are three cases. Redirect, flash, and unchanged tenant on a denied org switch are one case. Visiting the sign-in form and submitting it are one happy path, not two tests.

```ruby
# bad
test "requires name email and company" do
  customer = organizations(:northwind).customers.new
  refute customer.valid?
  assert_includes customer.errors[:name], "can't be blank"
  assert_includes customer.errors[:email], "can't be blank"
  assert_includes customer.errors[:company], "can't be blank"
end

test "sam cannot switch to northwind" do
  assert_redirected_to root_path
end

test "denied switch shows not authorized" do
  assert_select "#alert", text: "Not authorized"
end
```

```ruby
# good
test "requires name" do
  customer = organizations(:northwind).customers.new
  refute customer.valid?
  assert_includes customer.errors[:name], "can't be blank"
end

test "cannot switch to organization they are not a member of" do
  patch current_organization_path, params: { organization_id: organizations(:northwind).id }
  assert_redirected_to root_path
  follow_redirect!
  assert_select "#alert", text: "Not authorized"
  assert_select "aside p", text: "Globex"
end
```
